course: dictionary
lesson: 1596
title: Checkmate in chess and beyond
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Checkmate is a chess word, and you can work out its meaning from the words around it. «In chess the aim is checkmate, trapping the king, not capturing everything.» The clue is trapping the king: checkmate is about trapping, not about taking every piece.
explain: Test your idea by swapping it into the sentence. "In chess the aim is to trap the king so it cannot escape, not to capture everything." That still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Checkmate can be a noun, a verb, or a shout. A player says «Checkmate!» when they win. To checkmate someone means to win by trapping their king, and checkmates, checkmated and checkmating are the other forms of that verb.
explain: Outside chess, checkmate can mean someone is completely beaten or stuck. The sentence around it tells you which meaning the author wants.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Checkmate» means the king is attacked and cannot escape, so the game ends.
fact: «Check» means the king is attacked but can still escape.
fact: To checkmate someone is to win a chess game by trapping their king.
fact: Outside chess, checkmate can mean being completely beaten or stuck.
exercise: «In chess the aim is checkmate, trapping the king, not capturing everything.» What is the aim? | *Trapping the king so it cannot escape | Losing the game on purpose | Moving the queen first | Capturing as many pieces as possible
exercise: «In chess, learn how each piece moves; the aim is checkmate, not capturing everything.» What does checkmate mean? | Every piece has been taken | A piece moves two squares | The game is a draw | *The king is trapped and cannot escape
exercise: Players say «Check» and then «Checkmate!». What does «Check» mean? | The game is over and someone has lost | *The king is attacked but can still escape | The king has been taken | A piece is ready to move
test: Which word is a verb in «To checkmate someone is to win a chess game»? | game | *checkmate | chess | win
test: Someone says, «I was checkmated by my little brother at chess.» What does checkmated mean here? | Given a prize for playing well | Helped to win the game | *Trapped so the king could not escape, and beaten | Asked to play again
exam: Which sentence uses checkmate as a noun? | Checkmating is hard work for beginners | To checkmate the king, move the rook first | *In chess the aim is checkmate, trapping the king | Checkmated players sometimes laugh
